 "solutions": [
  {
   "question": "1",
   "part": null,
   "latex": "$f(x)=\\dfrac34(-x^2+8x-15)$, so $f'(x)=\\dfrac34(8-2x)$. The mode is where $f'(x)=0$: $8-2x=0$, so $x=4$. Answer (B).",
   "marks_breakdown": null,
   "source": "extracted"
  },
  {
   "question": "2",
   "part": null,
   "latex": "$\\displaystyle\\int_a^b g(x)\\,dx=\\int_a^b 2\\,dx-\\int_a^b f(x)\\,dx=[2x]_a^b-10=2b-2a-10=2(b-a-5)$. Answer (C).",
   "marks_breakdown": null,
   "source": "extracted"
  },
  {
   "question": "3",
   "part": null,
   "latex": "The line $y=3-x$ is the top curve and $y=e^{-x}$ the bottom, so the area is $\\displaystyle\\int_a^b (3-x-e^{-x})\\,dx$. Answer (A).",
   "marks_breakdown": null,
   "source": "extracted"
  },
  {
   "question": "4",
   "part": null,
   "latex": "$\\displaystyle\\int (2^x+e^x-e^{-x})\\,dx=\\dfrac{2^x}{\\ln 2}+e^x+e^{-x}+C$. Answer (B).",
   "marks_breakdown": null,
   "source": "extracted"
  },
  {
   "question": "5",
   "part": null,
   "latex": "$P(1\\le X\\le 4)=\\displaystyle\\int_1^4\\dfrac{\\pi}{12}\\sin\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi x}{6}\\right)dx=\\dfrac12\\left[-\\cos\\dfrac{\\pi x}{6}\\right]_1^4=\\dfrac12\\left[-\\cos\\dfrac{2\\pi}{3}+\\cos\\dfrac{\\pi}{6}\\right]=\\dfrac12\\left(\\dfrac12+\\dfrac{\\sqrt3}{2}\\right)=\\dfrac{1+\\sqrt3}{4}$. Answer (B).",
   "marks_breakdown": null,
   "source": "extracted"
  },
  {
   "question": "6",
   "part": null,
   "latex": "$\\displaystyle\\int_0^1(3-7x)^6dx=\\left[\\dfrac{(3-7x)^7}{-49}\\right]_0^1=\\dfrac{(-4)^7}{-49}-\\dfrac{3^7}{-49}=\\dfrac{16384}{49}+\\dfrac{2187}{49}=379$. Answer (C).",
   "marks_breakdown": null,
   "source": "extracted"
  },
  {
   "question": "7(a)",
   "part": "a",
   "latex": "Let $y=1-\\cos 2x$, so $y'=2\\sin 2x$.\n\n$$\\int\\dfrac{\\sin 2x}{1-\\cos 2x}\\,dx=\\dfrac12\\int\\dfrac{2\\sin 2x}{1-\\cos 2x}\\,dx=\\dfrac12\\ln(1-\\cos 2x)+C$$",
   "marks_breakdown": null,
   "source": "extracted"
  },
  {
   "question": "7(b)",
   "part": "b",
   "latex": "$$\\int\\left(x^2-x^{-2}+x^{1/3}\\right)dx=\\dfrac{x^3}{3}+x^{-1}+\\dfrac{3}{4}x^{4/3}+C=\\dfrac{x^3}{3}+\\dfrac1x+\\dfrac{3\\sqrt[3]{x^4}}{4}+C$$",
   "marks_breakdown": null,
   "source": "extracted"
  },
  {
